# Canonical author identities.
#
# `git log`, `git shortlog`, `git blame` and `git log --author=` resolve names and
# emails through this file, so a commit made under a stale identity is reported
# under the canonical one WITHOUT rewriting the commit object.
#
# emcrae@synoptek.com: a stale work address that agent worktrees on the primary
# dev box wrote into their per-worktree `author.email` (61 commits here, 170 in
# lotek core). The worktree configs are fixed; this maps the commits already
# written. GitHub resolves attribution by email at render time and does NOT read
# this file — the web UI is corrected separately, by moving the address between
# accounts. See ShyftXero/lotek#498.
Eli McRae <shyft@shyft.us> <emcrae@synoptek.com>

# Forensics note: once this mapping exists, `git log --author=emcrae@synoptek.com`
# matches NOTHING, because --author is applied to the mapped identity. To search the
# raw, as-written author field again, pass --no-use-mailmap. The commit objects are
# unchanged and still carry the original address; only the reporting is canonical.
